            <ArticleTitle>Drug-eluting stent-induced left anterior descending coronary artery aneurysm: repair by pericardial patch--where are we headed?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1530-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Deployment of drug-eluting stents has been associated with late thrombosis and restenosis on withdrawal of antiplatelet agents. We report a complication of inflammation and localized coronary artery aneurysms immediately adjacent to the stent after 4 years of implantation. Late chronic inflammatory responses may evolve for up to 4 years after sirolimus-eluting stent implantation and can cause weakening, erosion, and aneurysms of the coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
